      "id": 1,
      "text": "Lawrenceville takes its name from Captain James Lawrence, a naval officer who died during the War of 1812.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.experiencepa.com/the-historic-charm-of-pittsburghs-lawrenceville/",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Founded in 1982, the Lawrenceville Historical Society has dedicated itself to preserving and promoting the neighborhood’s rich history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.lawrencevillehistoricalsociety.org/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Historic homes and former factories line Lawrenceville’s streets, many now lofts or creative spaces that keep exposed brick and high ceilings.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9,
        10,
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.experiencepa.com/the-historic-charm-of-pittsburghs-lawrenceville/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Lawrenceville’s early growth hinged on its riverside location and railroad access, making it a 19th‑century industrial hub.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.experiencepa.com/the-historic-charm-of-pittsburghs-lawrenceville/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "In 2022 the LHS released the definitive history of the Allegheny Arsenal, the keystone that shaped Lawrenceville’s development.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.lawrencevillehistoricalsociety.org/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Lawrenceville sits at the crossroads of PA Route 287 and PA Route 49, where the town’s only traffic light waits.",
